{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/427375-modern-wars-and-stygia","id":427375,"title":"Modern Wars and Stygia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-03T21:25:29-08:00","id":427375,"title":"Modern Wars and Stygia","content":"I been thinking, how modern warfare and terrorism has affected stygia and such","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T08:59:33-08:00","id":427767,"title":"","content":"If you have the 6th Maelstrom going on.... not much?<br /> <br /> Otherwise? The Legion of Wrath gets more recruits? Some Heretic factions swell with new plasm? The Smiling Lord does a jig? You have to think of how a Relic IED would work or how to build one with a soulfire crystal? <br /> <br /> Or maybe, the answer is &quot;not very much at all in the grand scheme of things&quot;? Sure, NYC got a big glut of new wraiths in 9/11 and two wars have generated a fair total of wraiths of their own, but there has ALWAYS been war and death and people being simply awful to other people to the point of killing them, sometimes in large numbers.... Maybe those wars don't have the same gravitas as WWI, the Spanish Influenza or WWII.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T13:39:27-08:00","id":429231,"title":"","content":"I'm just hoping we don't see some unpleasant &quot;Heretic suicide bombers&quot; trash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T23:05:34-08:00","id":429888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/427375-modern-wars-and-stygia?p=429231#post429231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just hoping we don't see some unpleasant &amp;quot;Heretic suicide bombers&amp;quot; trash.</div> </div> </div> </div>One would think the very nature of the Shadowlands would preclude that sort of mentality. <br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T12:55:33-08:00","id":430524,"title":"","content":"The estimated hundreds of thousands killed in numerous events around the world for the &quot;war on terror&quot; don't quite have the same impact as 37 million dying in WWI, 60 million in WWII, and an estimated quarter million for the atomic bombs dropped on Japan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T09:56:51-07:00","id":432692,"title":"","content":"still, admit that would be interesting to see some &quot;War on Terror&quot; soldiers running next to allies while shooting at spectres...and using Drones (The military kind, not the supernatural beeings)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T09:58:39-07:00","id":434167,"title":"","content":"If it makes the Smiling Lord grin wider to feed newbie wraiths to Oblivion and waste some very valuable new Relics, sure, I guess...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T09:24:08-07:00","id":435821,"title":"","content":"In theory, there will be suicide bombers in the afterlife, sure. Unless they feel fulfilled, and thus either Transcend or reach Oblivion immediately. However, they'd be in for a big shock when they arrive in the Shadowlands. Perhaps they'll head to the Shadowlands of the Middle East to find their wraithly version of the Holy Land, and discover heathen wraiths (Anubis' bunch).<br /> <br /> It's always struck me as odd that there hasn't been much written about the Shadowlands of the Middle East, because Amenti is in the Tempest, and the dead of Christianity, Islam and Judaism in the region will have some serious issues to deal with once they cross the Shroud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T10:24:49-07:00","id":435896,"title":"","content":"Dansky himself confirmed months ago that he will touch upon the Shadowlands of the Middle East. If I remember correctly it is a part of Stygia.<br /> <br /> Also the Egyptian Dark Kingdom, or at least the ancient Egyptian one that's home to Anubis, is no longer connected to the Egyptian Shadowlands. It exists as its own realm of the Underworld. So its unlikely that a wraith would easily find it, much less stroll into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T11:45:10-07:00","id":437296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/427375-modern-wars-and-stygia?p=435896#post435896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dansky himself confirmed months ago that he will touch upon the Shadowlands of the Middle East. If I remember correctly it is a part of Stygia.<br /> <br /> Also the Egyptian Dark Kingdom, or at least the ancient Egyptian one that's home to Anubis, is no longer connected to the Egyptian Shadowlands. It exists as its own realm of the Underworld. So its unlikely that a wraith would easily find it, much less stroll into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. That's why I think something about the Shadowlands there (as opposed to Amenti) would be so interesting. <br /> <br /> Although, it seems a cop-out to make it simply part of the Dark Kingdom of Iron. Something that felt authentically Middle Eastern might be better. I mean, there's a huge legacy of Imperialm in the Middle East, but most of the Western Imperialism comes from the last few centuries, which is nothing for the dead. Stygian is older than the Crusades, after all, so something equally ancient might exist in the Middle East.<br /> <br /> Surely there are ancient Persian, Ottomon, Egyptian and Mesopotamian wraiths there that would have resisted an Empire that is, for all intents and purposes, modelled after the Classical world of Greece and Rome. The presence of religion is arguably also much stronger in the Middle East, and that would have some impact on what happens across the Shroud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 03-11-2015, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T11:48:22-07:00","id":437298,"title":"","content":"Of course, it'd be interesting to see the legacy of the Crusades, too. And what about the tunnels and passages running under the contested lands of the Gaza Strip? Then there are the Egyptians who didn't end up in Amenti. It's probably rife with material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 03-11-2015, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T12:51:25-07:00","id":437398,"title":"","content":"To paraphrase Buried Secrets, Stygian Legions followed the Roman Legions to the Middle East and never left. Cue the story hooks of the native wraiths raising insurrection against their Stygian oppressors. <br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T18:48:14-07:00","id":437863,"title":"","content":"Wraith Emperors seem to be very very good at taking territory and never, ever, ever loosening their grasp...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T23:43:17-07:00","id":438100,"title":"","content":"One thing I do know for sure: the recent destruction of ancient sites and more modern churches etc by ISIS is going to shred some fetters for some wraiths. Harrowings for some very, very old and potentially very powerful wraiths? That's a frightening thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T05:07:45-07:00","id":438286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/427375-modern-wars-and-stygia?p=437863#post437863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wraith Emperors seem to be very very good at taking territory and never, ever, ever loosening their grasp...</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean Xerxes rules the Shadowlands of the Middle East? *gets vision of the naked, bejewelled guy from 300 with thousands of thralls*<br /> <br /> That could be interesting...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T10:17:01-07:00","id":438647,"title":"","content":"I'd hazard to say, &quot;No.&quot; It seems like Iran/Persia is part of Stygia. which gives me more of a &quot;Alexander the Great&quot; vibe than Roman Empire. In which case Styiga can go all the way the Swar, covering modern Afghanistan and Pakistan. So, if there is a &quot;Dark Kingdom of &lt;fill in the blank&gt;&quot; remnant of Persia, it's probably like Egypt vis-a-vis Amenti/the Dark Kingdom of Sand, in that it's there/not there. <br /> <br /> I don't know if W20 is going to deal with how Dark Kingdom's &quot;overlap&quot;, particularly Stygia, since it seems like imperialist expansions stacked on top of another - out from Europe subsuming, North, South, Central America, Near and Middle East and North Africa? (If you give the Middle East and Egypt to Stygia, you gotta give it the rest of super-Saharan Africa). <br /> <br /> Maybe somewhere Xsayarsa/Xerxes/Ahashverosh is still in charge. It might have certain values of increased coolness if Ancient Persia was still in control of the adjacent Shadowlands instead of something akin to Amenti.... It does make particular sense in that case, as, up to the most recent Shahanshah, the local feeling of self-identity existed through the succession of dynasties all the way back to the Achmaenids, somewhat similar to Han &quot;identity&quot; in China going back to the Qin/Han Dynasties. <br /> <br /> If you can find some good sources on the Persian view of the Underworld, it might be cool to mock something up even if the area is given over to Stygia in RAW. For fan use and/or to base a good non-Shadowlands contiguous Dark Kingdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T08:57:45-07:00","id":439986,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that would be particularly cool, and would feel more authentic than having it be yet another outpost of Stygia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}